
	Speed gained:

		fptk v0.4.4 took around 1200 ms to load (so slow):
		-  80 ms — hy (not fptk issue, this is what it is)
		- 400 ms — hyrule (very long load for some reason, not fptk issue) 
		- 800 ms — funcs, pydantic, monads, etc.

		fptk v0.5.0 loads at:
		-  80 ms — hy 
		-  50 ms — extracted hyrule macros   \
		-  50 ms — funcs                     | core load times
		-  50 ms — all macros, including lns /
		-  50 ms — (optional) lenses lib (import lenses [lens])
		- 120 ms — (optional) strict-typing = pydantic load time
		- 120 ms — (optional) monads; for some reason BaseClass is slow to load (even when pydantic is already loaded) 
		// overall time is around: 200 ms core, +250 ms lenses+pydantic+monads

		other 3rd party libs:
		-  15 ms — funcy
		-   1 ms — termcolor
		-   0 ms — operator, math, os ... and all the basic libs

	Implemented measures to increase startup time:
		
		// ↑ strong speed increase
		• Removed hyrule dependency (kept only required hyrule-macros in new module) // 0.400 ms → 0.030 ms

		• For this costly operation: hy.read(hy.eval(... :macros * :readers *)) 
		  - removed «:readers» arg in __init__ // x2 execution time reduction
		  - all macroses are loaded in one go (from one main module)

		• Removed scattering of (require fptk.macros [f::]) all over the files.
		  // 100 separate «require» costs 700 ms to load (even after compiling)
		  // 1 require (with 100 macros together) is about 30 ms

		• Clumped everything in few files
		  // import  time: 1 big file is 50 ms to load, 10 files are 80 ms;
		  // require time: even worth

		• Made lens/pydantic/monads to be separate modules, not loaded by default

